From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 05:58:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rust-target-config: fix invalid +v5/+v5te LLVM feature for
 armv5 tunes

llvm_features_from_tune() emits "+v5te" or "+v5" for armv5-family
tunes, but LLVM's ARM backend has no such feature names -- only
"v5t" (confirmed via `rustc --print target-features`). The invalid
token is silently dropped ("... is not a recognized feature for this
target (ignoring feature)"), so the generated rust target spec ends
up with no ARM architecture-version feature at all. Combined with
"+thumb-mode" (correctly requested since these tunes build with
-mthumb), LLVM then has no basis to know the target supports Thumb,
and compiler_builtins' inline `.thumb` asm fails to build:

    error: <inline asm>:5:1: target does not support Thumb mode
    error: could not compile `compiler_builtins` (lib)

Hit building domoticz-image for an armv5te qemuarm machine (Angstrom's
kas/qemuarm-armv5te.yml sets DEFAULTTUNE = "armv5te").

The `if 'armv5te' in feat` branch was also dead code: TUNE_FEATURES
never contains the literal string "armv5te" (see
conf/machine/include/arm/arch-armv5-dsp.inc) -- only the
ARMPKGARCH/tune name uses it, TUNE_FEATURES itself is "arm armv5
thumb dsp". So every armv5-family tune always fell through to the
"+v5" branch regardless.

Collapse both branches into one that emits the real "+v5t" feature;
"dsp" is already applied separately a few lines down.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
---
 meta/classes-recipe/rust-target-config.bbclass | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/meta/classes-recipe/rust-target-config.bbclass b/meta/classes-recipe/rust-target-config.bbclass
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/meta/classes-recipe/rust-target-config.bbclass
+++ b/meta/classes-recipe/rust-target-config.bbclass
@@ -48,12 +48,14 @@ def llvm_features_from_tune(d):

     if ('armv6' in mach_overrides) or ('armv6' in feat):
         f.append("+v6")
-    if 'armv5te' in feat:
-        f.append("+strict-align")
-        f.append("+v5te")
-    elif 'armv5' in feat:
+    # LLVM's ARM feature table has no "v5te"/"v5" token, only "v5t"
+    # (verify with `rustc --print target-features`); dsp is handled
+    # separately below. The old 'armv5te' in feat branch was dead code:
+    # TUNE_FEATURES never contains that literal string, only the
+    # ARMPKGARCH/tune name does.
+    if 'armv5' in feat:
         f.append("+strict-align")
-        f.append("+v5")
+        f.append("+v5t")

     if ('armv4' in mach_overrides) or ('armv4' in feat):
         f.append("+strict-align")
--
2.43.0
